From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] CP15: the ARM9 region timings saturate at a byte (core.arm9_mhz past the DSi clock)

At ARM9ClockShift 4 and up, bus costs shifted into the u8 table wrapped round to next to nothing.
---
--- a/src/CP15.cpp
+++ b/src/CP15.cpp
@@ -314,6 +314,8 @@
     // (the same bytes as before, a 4-byte store per entry: written byte by byte through u8s, which may alias anything,
     // every entry loaded the clock shift and the bus timings again; 1M entries for a whole rebuild took ~12 ms on an A55)
     const u32 shift = NDS.ARM9ClockShift;
+    // (a byte each: past the DSi's clock - core.arm9_mhz - a slow bus's cost would wrap round to next to nothing)
+    const auto cost = [shift](u8 c) { const u32 v = (u32)c << shift; return (u8)(v > 0xFF ? 0xFF : v); };
     for (u32 i = addrstart; i < addrend; i++)
     {
         const u8 pu = PU_Map[i];
@@ -323,7 +325,7 @@
         if (pu & 0x40)
             t[0] = 0xFF;//kCodeCacheTiming;
         else
-            t[0] = bustimings[2] << shift;
+            t[0] = cost(bustimings[2]);
 
         if (pu & 0x10)
         {
@@ -333,9 +335,9 @@
         }
         else
         {
-            t[1] = bustimings[0] << shift;
-            t[2] = bustimings[2] << shift;
-            t[3] = bustimings[3] << shift;
+            t[1] = cost(bustimings[0]);
+            t[2] = cost(bustimings[2]);
+            t[3] = cost(bustimings[3]);
         }
         memcpy(MemTimings[i], t, 4);
     }
